# extension/config.js used to be ignored. It is committed now: the watchlist
# page is a static site and has to ship the project URL and publishable key in
# its files regardless, so a hidden second copy bought nothing. Both values are
# designed to be public — the key grants nothing without a signed-in owner.
#
# What must never be committed is a key beginning sb_secret_, a service_role
# key, or a database password. Those bypass every rule in the database.
